/* librt stub for Android (bionic).
 *
 * WHY THIS EXISTS
 * ---------------
 * native/src/beetle-pce/Makefile adds `-lrt` unconditionally on every
 * non-Haiku platform (Makefile:80, :126, :153, :343, :356). Glibc needs
 * that: it is where clock_gettime, timer_create and the POSIX realtime
 * functions live. Android's bionic does not ship librt at all -- those
 * functions are in libc -- so the link fails with
 *
 *     cannot find -lrt: No such file or directory
 *
 * and the cardcon core cannot be built for android-arm64, which is one
 * reason android tops out at 7 bundled cores against desktop's 11.
 *
 * WHAT THIS IS
 * ------------
 * A GNU ld LINKER SCRIPT named librt.so, not a compiled object. The
 * linker only wants a file by that name to satisfy `-lrt`; it needs no
 * symbols FROM it, because every symbol the core actually calls is
 * already in libc. `INPUT(-lc)` makes the dependency explicit rather
 * than relying on the linker's implicit search, and an empty
 * `GROUP`/`OUTPUT` body means the archive contributes no definitions --
 * so this can never shadow a real libc symbol. That is the whole safety
 * argument: the stub satisfies the *name*, and adds nothing.
 *
 * Verified, not assumed: clock_gettime is declared in the NDK sysroot's
 * usr/include/time.h, and the NDK has no librt.so anywhere. See
 * test/android_stub_test.dart, which asserts both the file exists and
 * that a link against it resolves clock_gettime from libc.
 *
 * This file is referenced from scripts/build_core.sh:299, which puts
 * this directory on LIBRARY_PATH for android builds only.
 */
INPUT(-lc)
